  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale:** Our approach combines multi-resolution optimization with physics-inspired constraints to escape local minima. We start from the parent solution and steer the optimization away from shallow overlaps by introducing two key innovations:  \n   a) **Frequency-targeted mutation:** We enforce minimal correlation across specific frequency bands by penalizing overlapping patterns near the critical Fourier modes where the parent solution shows strong spectral leakage.  \n   b) **Gradient tilting:** During optimization, we artificially shift the gradient toward regions where the overlap is increasing at high-frequency lags.  \n   This differs from previous strategies by explicitly targeting the spectral characteristics of the overlap instead of relying solely on gradient descent. We expect this to find solutions with cleaner boundaries between active and inactive regions, which inherently reduces overlap.\n\n2. **Mathematical specification:**  \n   Variables:\n   - N: grid size (190, 380, 760)  \n   - h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f vector with \u2211h\u1d62 = N/2  \n   - dx = 2/N  \n   - C\u2085 = max\u2096 (1/\u2211\u2c7c |h\u2096 \u2297 (1-h)\u2096|) * dx    [full cross-correlation]  \n\n   Objectives:\n   - Minimize C\u2085 using a penalized objective:\n     \u2211\u2096 w\u2096 \u00b7 [5] \u00b7 (1/\u2211\u2097\u208b\u2081 l\u2097) + \u222b |h*(1-h)|\u00b2 dk  \n   where w\u2096 weights high-frequency lags (k > N/3)\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Boundary enforcement: h\u2080, h\u2099 restricted to avoid edge artifacts\n   - Momentum regularization: \u222b |h''(x)|\u00b2 dx \u2264 C\u2098\u2099  \n   - Used solver:Conditional Mean-Field with Lagrange Projection (CMFL)\n\n3. **Implementation procedure:**\n   a) Initialize grids: [190, 380] (dx=0.01,0.005)\n   b) For each grid N:\n      i) Start with interpolated parent\n      ii) Apply N-times longer optimization phase than previous method\n      iii) Maintain multi-scale persistence vectors\n      iv) Compute gradients using staggered correlation layers\n      v) Project solutions using mean-field annealing\n\n4. **Search choices and variations:**  \n   - Grid progression: 190 * scale factor (start scale=1, expand to 2)\n   - Gradient weighting: Pareto-optimal contribution from 10 Lag groups\n   - Mutation probability: Piecewise logistic function based on overlap history\n\n5. **Budget and robustness:**  \n   - Grid sizes processed: 190 and 380\n   - Total evaluations: ~2000 per grid (yielding 4000 total)\n   - Fallback solution from grid 190 if grid 380 fails time\n\n6. **Validation and return contract:**  \n   - Validates 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 with clipping projection\n   - Recomputes C\u2085 using numpy.correlate with duplicates\n   - Returns (best_h, final_C5, grid_size)",
